1
00:00:00,203 --> 00:00:09,511
1. A teacher creates a classroom and reuses existing LabTwin authentication.

2
00:00:09,511 --> 00:00:19,625
2. Courses remain attached to classrooms. Student access is restricted to enrolled classrooms.

3
00:00:19,625 --> 00:00:29,576
3. A real PDF upload is automatically indexed. Citations open the exact source page.

4
00:00:29,576 --> 00:00:38,802
4. Demo Mode processes an original textbook PDF, slide deck and embedded-caption lecture into one knowledge base.

5
00:00:38,802 --> 00:00:47,852
5. Ask LabTwin retrieves course-backed information with page, slide and timestamp citations.

6
00:00:47,852 --> 00:00:57,005
6. The lecture citation seeks to the original timestamp. Embedded captions were extracted automatically; this fixture has no spoken narration.

7
00:00:57,005 --> 00:01:06,107
7. Diagram understanding uses native connector relationships: new node points to previous head. The source figure is preserved.

8
00:01:06,107 --> 00:01:15,391
8. Off-material questions are declined. LabTwin does not present outside knowledge as a course-backed answer.

9
00:01:15,391 --> 00:01:24,705
9. A verified, source-cited diagnostic question records a real answer and updates the Bayesian learner model.

10
00:01:24,705 --> 00:01:33,860
10. The actual C program fails hidden checks. The likely concept is preserving the old head connection; private test cases remain hidden.

11
00:01:33,860 --> 00:01:43,151
11. Progressive hints move from an invariant to specific reasoning, with source recommendations.

12
00:01:43,151 --> 00:01:52,556
12. Successful retesting changes mastery. The follow-up explains why this question was selected. This demo teacher explicitly allows full examples.

13
00:01:52,556 --> 00:02:01,888
13. The mastery map links prerequisites and subtopics. Clicking a topic exposes history, mistakes and source resources.

14
00:02:01,888 --> 00:02:11,083
14. Scoped MCQ, short-answer and numerical assessments provide cited feedback and post-assessment mastery reports.

15
00:02:11,083 --> 00:02:20,771
15. Viva asks follow-ups based on work and prior answers. Provisional feedback is available for teacher review; activity signals never prove cheating.

16
00:02:20,771 --> 00:02:34,664
16. Teacher insights expose supporting student evidence, before/after mastery and CSV reports.

17
00:02:34,664 --> 00:02:43,707
17. DeepEval actually executes the team benchmark and three four-session learner simulations. Offline metrics are labelled proxies; model-estimated gains are not claimed as causal human learning gains.

18
00:02:43,707 --> 00:03:13,654
Personalization evidence grows across sessions. Next-answer prediction loss, model uncertainty, difficulty progression and repetition are computed from actual simulated responses. These are controlled experiments, not a human study.
